    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "Daniel sees the Lord and others in a glorious vision—He is shown what is to be in the latter days.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "In the third year of Cyrus king of Persia a thing was revealed unto Daniel, whose name was called Belteshazzar; and the thing was true, but the time appointed was long: and he understood the thing, and had understanding of the vision.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 206,
            "end": 219,
            "text": "Dan. 1:17 (6–20)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 129
          },
          {
            "start": 159,
            "end": 162
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 10:1",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "In those days I Daniel was mourning three full weeks.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "Alma 17:3 (3, 9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 10:2",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "I ate no pleasant bread, neither came flesh nor wine in my mouth, neither did I anoint myself at all, till three whole weeks were fulfilled.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "HEB desirable foods."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 10:3",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And in the four and twentieth day of the first month, as I was by the side of the great river, which is Hiddekel;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "IE the Tigris."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 103
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
