        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 10:9",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And, behold, an hand touched me, which set me upon my knees and upon the palms of my hands.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 10:10",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And he said unto me, O Daniel, a man greatly beloved, understand the words that I speak unto thee, and stand upright: for unto thee am I now sent. And when he had spoken this word unto me, I stood trembling.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "D&C 7:1 (1, 5)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Daniel 10:11",
        "book": "Daniel",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Then said he unto me, Fear not, Daniel: for from the first day that thou didst set thine heart to understand, and to chasten thyself before thy God, thy words were heard, and I am come for thy words.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "Luke 1:13 (12–13); Hel. 5:26; D&C 68:6; 98:1; JS—H 1:32."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "Dan. 9:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 132,
            "text": "HEB humble thyself."
          },
          {
            "start": 164,
            "end": 169,
            "text": "Mosiah 9:18; 27:14; Abr. 1:16 (15–16)."
          }
        ],
